<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI25-RBQA-F002-new>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI25-RBQA-F002-new" ;
  triage:title "lint_boundaries.py never validates the [ownership]/io_forbidden table, so forbidden-dependency violations like AI25-RBQA-F001 are invisible to the mechanical boundary gate" ;
  triage:description "Reported by ruthless-boundary-qa during AICH-S5-QA-2 (AI.25 fix-round-2 recheck, PR #640, commit 5f794c42d449687b6badca46193592f11bc25529, branch feature/pAI-s25-peer-authority-resolution), as a companion finding to AI25-RBQA-F001 (a boundary policy leak that the mechanical gate failed to catch). The boundary-enforcement lint script (locate it -- likely lint_boundaries.py or similar under scripts/ or .claude/) does not validate declared [ownership]/io_forbidden tables in adapter boundary TOML files (e.g. peer-http-adapter.toml), meaning policy violations like resolve_peer_authority living in a forbidden file for recipient_routing are not mechanically caught. Multiple boundary TOML files declare [ownership]/io_forbidden tables (peer-http-adapter.toml and others in boundaries/ directory), but lint_boundaries.py does not check that code-level implementations respect these forbidden-dependency declarations. The lint script's REQUIRED_BOUNDARY_FIELDS tuple does not include ('ownership', 'io_forbidden'), and no validation function exists to check io_forbidden entries against actual source code patterns." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "FTQ" ;
  triage:severity "Minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T12:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S5 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T16:26:33Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI25-RBQA-F002-new/lint-gap-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI25-RBQA-F002-new/pAI-s25/96377687> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

# 2026-07-26 (quality-mgr, AICH-S5-QA-5): PARTIALLY fixed on feature/pAI-s25-peer-authority-resolution
# @ 96377687 (PR #640). lint_boundaries.py now validates ownership.io_owns/io_forbidden as
# well-formed, non-empty string lists (schema-shape only). Independently confirmed by
# ruthless-boundary-qa that there is still NO generic mapping from io_forbidden tag values
# (recipient_routing, sqlite, delivery_queue, retry_state, nudge_emission, ...) to source-code
# patterns checked against the owning module -- the only thing catching the AI25-RBQA-F004 leak
# class is a single hardcoded AST test (boundary_enforcement.rs::
# ai25_peer_authority_selection_is_not_owned_by_the_https_adapter), not a general mechanism.
# Kept OPEN (not closed) -- reclassified as the narrower "lint_gap: io_forbidden not semantically
# enforced" scope requested in the finding's own title.

